# Regression for the index-based-terminal explain fault — configflux-autp.
#
# The kv5d suite above uses only hand-rolled BDD fixtures whose non-terminal
# nodes reference ⊥/⊤ via the sentinel constants. The real oxidd/cudd
# compiler serializer instead references the terminals BY TABLE INDEX
# (0 = ⊥, 1 = ⊤ per ADR-0005 §4; see compiler `ccm_emitter/bdd.rs::child_id`),
# which made `explain_rejection`'s falsifying-path walker fault on EVERY
# real-model `.ccm`. This test drives `explain_rejection` over a `.ccm` whose
# BDD uses that index-based terminal convention (the same on-disk shape
# `load_ccm_real_fixture` round-trips), asserting a labeled core for a
# forbidden option and Ok-with-no-core for a valid one — without depending on
# the compiler crate (ADR-0003 §2).
rust_test(
    name = "explain_rejection_real_ccm_test",
    size = "small",
    timeout = "short",
    srcs = [
        "tests/explain_rejection_real_ccm.rs",
        "tests/fixture_v2.rs",
    ],
    crate_root = "tests/explain_rejection_real_ccm.rs",
    edition = "2021",
    deps = [
        ":solver",
        "@crates//:serde",
        "@crates//:serde_json",
        "@crates//:sha2",
    ],
)

